~06ออออ~0Eอออ ~0FHOW TO PLAY ~0Eออออออออ~06ออออออออออออออออออออออ

~0FTic-Tac-Toe~07, or ~0FNoughts and Crosses~07, is played
on a ~0F3 x 3~07 board. The players take turns putting
their mark, ~0FO~07 or ~0FX~07, on an empty square; ~0FO
always goes first. The first to get ~0Ethree in a
~0Erow~07, across, down or diagonally, wins. When
the board is full with no row, it is a ~0Etie~07.

Played well by both sides, every game is a tie.

~02ออออ~0Aอออ ~0FGAME MODES ~0Aออออออออ~02อออออออออออออออออออออออ

 ~0E* ~0FVS HUMAN~07: two players at one keyboard.
 ~0E* ~0FVS AI~07: you play ~0FO~07, the computer plays ~0FX~07:
   ~0Feasy~07 grabs a win it can see but little
   else, ~0Fmedium~07 also blocks your wins, and
   ~0Fhard~07 thinks every game to the end: it
   never loses.

The wins of each side and the ties are counted
for as long as the game runs.

~01ออออ~09อออ ~0FCONTROLS ~09ออออออออ~01อออออออออออออออออออออออออ

 ~0E* ~0FMove the cursor~08 . . . . ~0BArrows~07 or ~0BW A S D
 ~0E* ~0FPut your mark~08 . . . . . ~0ASPACE~07 or ~0AENTER
 ~0E* ~0FHelp / about~08. . . . . . ~09H~07 / ~09?
 ~0E* ~0FLeave the game~08. . . . . ~0CESC

After a game, ~0ASPACE~07 or ~0AENTER~07 starts the next.

~05ออออ~0Dอออ ~0FOPTIONS ~0Dออออออออ~05ออออออออออออออออออออออออออ

 ~0E* ~0FUse heart icon~07: hearts instead of noughts.
